The Weaver grew lonely and despondent. She wove more frantically, trying to create something that would last, but the void consumed everything. One evening, exhausted and heartbroken, she wept over her loom. Her tears fell onto her latest tapestry—a cloth woven from threads of pure light.

Where each tear touched the fabric, it burned a tiny hole, and the light began to shine through. Instead of fading, these pinpricks of brilliance held fast against the darkness. Amazed, the Weaver cast her tear-stained tapestry across the entire sky, and where her tears had fallen, eternal lights blazed forth.

